Virtual Inheritance

📌 Description

This C++ program demonstrates Multiple Inheritance and Virtual Inheritance using four classes:

- "Person"
- "Student"
- "Employee"
- "TeachingAssistant"

The "TeachingAssistant" class inherits from both "Student" and "Employee", while both classes virtually inherit from "Person".

Virtual inheritance ensures that only one shared copy of the "Person" base class exists in "TeachingAssistant".

