🧠 OOP Concept Used

Virtual Inheritance

Virtual inheritance is used to solve the Diamond Problem in multiple inheritance.

          Person
         /      \
   Student    Employee
         \      /
     TeachingAssistant

Without virtual inheritance, "TeachingAssistant" could contain two copies of "Person"—one through "Student" and another through "Employee".

By using:

class Student : virtual public Person

and

class Employee : virtual public Person

only one shared "Person" base-class subobject is created.

